## 10.1 DEFAULT PRESENT SYSTEM

The system must automatically generate attendance records for every active student on configured school working days.

Default status: PRESENT.

However, the attendance record must remain marked as pending verification until the authorized teacher verifies and finalizes the class attendance.

Teachers should only need to change the status of students who are absent, late, on leave, or half-day.

Important rules:

- Do not generate attendance on weekends.
- Do not generate attendance on holidays.
- Allow administrators to configure working days.
- Allow administrators to manage holidays and school-closed dates.
- Prevent duplicate attendance records.
- Maintain attendance edit history.
- Do not overwrite finalized records without authorized correction.
- Show classes with pending attendance verification.
- Approved leave must be distinguishable from unexplained absence.

## 10.2 AUTOMATIC CONSECUTIVE ABSENCE ALERT

VERY IMPORTANT:

